  "summary": "The paper proposes a hybrid QC+GenAI credit fraud detection framework and reports 97.8% accuracy, 2.3% false-positive rate, 3.1% false-negative rate, and 27 ms latency for the proposed model. A standalone QSVM is also reported at 95.3% accuracy, 4.0% FPR, 5.2% FNR, and 41 ms latency, compared with a Random Forest baseline at 91.6% accuracy, 6.8% FPR, 8.2% FNR, and 72 ms latency. No specific quantum hardware, qubit count, or circuit-depth data are provided, and no practical quantum advantage is demonstrated.",
